rows.prompt:
Operation: SET_TITLE - Set the note title
Arguments: {"title": string}
Request: change the title to "Write-ahead logs make crash recovery boring"

Operation: SET_DESCRIPTION - Set the note description (max 200 chars)
Arguments: {"description": string}
Request: the one-liner under the heading should read: Batching fsyncs trades a few milliseconds of latency for an order of magnitude more throughput.

Operation: SET_NOTE_TYPE - Set or change the note type
Arguments: {"noteType": "concept" | "decision" | "pattern" | "observation" | "procedure" | "architecture" | "bug-pattern" | "integration" | "workflow" | "reference"}
Request: set the note type to decision

Operation: SET_CONTENT - Replace the markdown content body
Arguments: {"content": string}
Request: wipe what's written here and put this in its place: Compaction debt grows faster than write volume once L0 has more than eight files.

Operation: ADD_TOPIC - Tag the note with a topic
Arguments: {"name": string}
Request: add the topic "storage engines" to this

Operation: SET_METADATA_FIELD - Set any string metadata field by name
Arguments: {"field": "scope" | "confidence" | "severity" | "editor" | "modelId" | "version" | "filePath" | "computes" | "context" | "decisionStatus" | "model" | "sourceType" | "targetType" | "relationType" | "cardinality" | "errorMessage" | "rootCause" | "correctPattern"}
Request: we're not very sure about this one yet, only a single benchmark backs it, so call our certainty low

Operation: SET_METADATA_LIST_FIELD - Set any string-array metadata field by name
Arguments: {"field": "models" | "hooksUsed" | "dispatchTargets" | "modules" | "inputs" | "outputs" | "consumedBy" | "alternatives" | "consequences", "values": string[]}
Request: set the consequences to: slower cold start, roughly 2x disk usage

Operation: ARCHIVE_NOTE - Transition CANONICAL → ARCHIVED
Arguments: {"comment": string}
Request: archive this note, the newer compaction writeup replaces it

Operation: CREATE_MOC - Initialize a new Map of Content
Arguments: {"tier": "DOMAIN" | "HUB" | "TOPIC", "title": string, "description": string, "orientation": string}
Request: create a domain-level map called "Observability". Description: everything about logs, metrics and traces. Orientation: start with the three pillars, then read the cost notes.

Operation: UPDATE_ORIENTATION - Update the synthesis paragraph
Arguments: {"orientation": string}
Request: the bit at the top that tells readers where to begin should say: Read the incident reviews first, then the alerting notes.

Operation: UPDATE_DESCRIPTION - Update the progressive disclosure summary
Arguments: {"description": string}
Request: update the description to "Notes on alert fatigue and on-call health"

Operation: ADD_CORE_IDEA - Add a note to Core Ideas with context phrase
Arguments: {"noteRef": string, "contextPhrase": string, "sortOrder": number}
Request: add "SLOs beat static thresholds" as a core idea, it's the reason we moved off fixed CPU alerts

Operation: ADD_OPEN_QUESTION - Add an unexplored direction
Arguments: {"question": string}
Request: add an open question: do we page on error-budget burn or on raw symptoms?

Operation: ADD_CHILD_MOC - Add a child MOC reference
Arguments: {"childRef": string}
Request: the "Alert routing" map should sit underneath this one

Operation: SET_METADATA_FIELD - Set a whitelisted string metadata field on the MoC. Currently only `version`, which records the Powerhouse stack release the MoC's knowledge is registered against.
Arguments: {"field": "version"}
Request: set the version to 2.1

Operation: INGEST_SOURCE - Add new source material
Arguments: {"sourceType": "ARTICLE" | "BOOK_CHAPTER" | "CONVERSATION" | "DOCUMENTATION" | "MANUAL_ENTRY" | "PAPER" | "TRANSCRIPT" | "WEB_PAGE", "title": string, "content": string}
Request: ingest this paper: "The Tail at Scale" by Jeffrey Dean and Luiz Barroso, https://research.google/pubs/the-tail-at-scale/ - content: Latency variability across many servers dominates request latency at scale; hedged and tied requests reduce the tail.

Operation: INGEST_SOURCE - Add new source material
Arguments: {"sourceType": "ARTICLE" | "BOOK_CHAPTER" | "CONVERSATION" | "DOCUMENTATION" | "MANUAL_ENTRY" | "PAPER" | "TRANSCRIPT" | "WEB_PAGE", "title": string, "content": string}
Request: here's the transcript from Tuesday's architecture call, file it as "Arch sync 2026-10-13": Sam: we keep the old queue until the backfill ends. Priya: agreed, and we cut over shard by shard.

